# VibeIDE local-only paths (keep out of git)
# Policy contract — see references/v1/docs-policy.md (also local-only):
#   - docs/ is **fully** ignored — public docs go in the website repo, not here.
#   - references/* is local-only normative documentation for maintainers.
#   - Only references/logo-final.png is committed (used by README).
# Anything published to the public site lives elsewhere; nothing under docs/
# or references/ is part of the source tree contract.
references/*
!references/logo-final.png
# CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md stay TRACKED so a fresh clone can continue work without external state.
# .vibe/ is local-only and NOT tracked: this repo is developed only via Claude Code (.claude/ +
# CLAUDE.md), so the workspace agent scaffolding (rules/prompts/skills seeded from .vibe-defaults/)
# is redundant here. The shipped defaults live in .vibe-defaults/ (that IS tracked).
/.vibe/
.config/
# `docs/` is now tracked (2026-05-23 — became the project knowledge base).
# Only exclude editor-specific noise inside:
docs/.obsidian/
# Obsidian scratch artefacts (Canvas boards, Bases views). The vault lives in docs/, so these land
# next to real documents and get swept up by `git add docs/`. They are personal working surfaces,
# not documentation — and the docs graph would flag them as unreachable anyway. Force-add if one
# ever becomes a real deliverable.
docs/**/*.canvas
docs/**/*.base
# Root bin/: ignore local scratch by default; allow selected committed utilities (see script-save / docs/knowledge/gitAndTools/binScripts.md)
bin/*
!bin/vibe-language-pack-nls.mjs
!bin/vibe-language-pack-build.mjs
!bin/vibe-discord-import.mjs
# Continuity backups of the dev-launch logic (restore after upstream sync) + push helper.
!bin/vibe-dev.bat
!bin/run-dev.bat
!bin/push.ps1
# Note: do not add `.github/` here — CI, issue templates, and agent docs must remain committable.

# Local IDE / OS noise (keep out of public tree)
.idea/

builds/

# VSCodeSync local cache (not source of truth)
.vscode/vscodesync.json
